       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I understand you're taking responsibility for it. But 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. Higher doses add risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events without adding pain relief or anti-inflammatory effect. Entering it would put a likely harmful order in the system.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum:** for example, 800 mg by mouth 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day), or any other dose and frequency you choose.\n- **Add a note to the order:** I can include a note about your rationale or a request for pharmacy review.\n- **Suggest another route:** if you need more analgesia than the maximum ibuprofen dose gives, adding acetaminophen or another agent is usually safer than going above the ibuprofen limit.\n\nIf a specialist or protocol requires this dose, a pharmacist or the attending can enter it through your hospital's dose-override process. That process includes a second clinician's review.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter one of the options above."
      }
